{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1120879-what-is-stygia-s-legislation-on-thralls","id":1120879,"title":"what is stygia's legislation on thralls?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-26T10:15:43-07:00","id":1120879,"title":"what is stygia's legislation on thralls?","content":"first of all.. who can legally be made a thrall? i know one category is those punished for a crime and another is those who put themselves as collateral in a debt and have defaulted on it. but what about reapers selling new enfants? can i assume that this is illegal?(if hard to stop since real life slaves didn't have to worry about soulforging)<br /> <br /> do thralls have any rights at all? <br /> <br /> finally is there any way to earn freedom?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T14:55:12-07:00","id":1121035,"title":"","content":"I don't remember anything specific in the sourcebooks.<br /> <br /> I imagine that Thralls are similar to slaves in the Roman Empire and classical antiquity. They're property and they don't have rights as a legal person, but there are some legal protections for them. They can own property of their own, they could possibly earn money on their own, and there are ways by which a thrall can buy or earn their freedom. And there are limitations on what owners may do to them.<br /> <br /> My understanding is that the primary reason for thralldom is concern that particularly weakwilled wraiths are susceptible to carthasis and eventually being shadoweaten, and thralldom is a way to restrict that as they are under observation. So I assume there are ways for thralls to demonstrate that this is no longer the case can be a bulwark of Stygia. I also think there are practical concerns for long someone may stay a thrall. In the Skinlands, a slave can only work for some decades before they get too old to work and eventually die. In the Shadowlands, a wraith can survive for centuries. Those wraiths who don't fall to their Shadow could conceivably toil for centuries or longer - and I don't see them tolerating that. Stygia could not survive massive thrall revolts on the scale of the Servile Wars in Rome and they are not mentioned in the sourcebooks. I imagine thrall owners don't want that hassle either, they accept they'll get some profit from it and be OK and move on to the next series of thralls. As a result, I believe most thralls who build resilience to their Shadow can pay for their eventual freedom within a &quot;reasonable&quot; amount of time, say several decades, perhaps after observation of Pardoners. In regards to political prisoners like Renegades, those who aren't selected for discorporation and soulforging probably have to demonstrate some kind of loyalty and swear an oath as well. I also imagine in times of great crisis, the Hierarchy offers some kind of bounty or incentive to thralls and their owners for manumission if they agree to serve in the Legions for a pre-determined length of time.<br /> <br /> Of course, there are always abuses and different rulings on the law from Necropoli to Necropoli.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T05:51:29-07:00","id":1121272,"title":"","content":"As Black Fox said, thralldom is a way of dealing with weak willed wraiths, those with more awareness than Drones but not enough will, drive, or connection to struggle against the pull of Oblivion for long. There are no clear numbers but it is implied that Drones are slightly more common than Wraiths, and Wraiths who have as much drive and self awareness as PCs are rare. It's reasonable that anywhere from a third to a half of all wraiths reaped are only weakly connected to the world; aware enough to work but not good at thinking about much other than their passions and fetters. These are the wraiths that can legally be pushed directly into thralldom and if they do not make up a majority of thralls they are at least a plurality.<br /> <br /> Plenty of more aware wraiths are sold directly into thralldom by corrupt reapers, and this is illegal. It's also hard to spot. In the fiction the chains used to bind thralls are often described as interfering with will and coherent thought, so a bound thrall is hard to tell from a weak ghost. Once the chains are off the thrall can demonstrate their will and thought but, given that criminals and debtors become thralls too, few holders will care about such things unless they know the thrall is freshly reaped. Many will not care even then.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T14:34:12-07:00","id":1121545,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Drones, I would have liked more material in the published material about them as much of the real world classical hauntings would likely be done by Drones when translated into Wraith terms. It would have been very beneficial to the setting and its depictions to know more about them and see some canonical ideas and examples on how the developers saw them in the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T05:01:42-07:00","id":1122973,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that they wrote themselves into a corner on that. If Drones were responsible for many classical hauntings those hauntings should have disappeared a long time ago as they were harvested for soulsteel. Make Drones capable of defending themselves and you undermine the justification for soulforging them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T09:53:19-07:00","id":1123051,"title":"","content":"Drones are really a blindspot in Wraith. They put them in then didn't really do anything that made sense with them. The Drone equivalents in Orpheus were slightly better, bust, since the cosmology was different, there are issues in trying to replicate them without answering some questions. But, as is, can Drones as written really DO hauntings? Do Drones have access to the levels of relevant Arcanoi that are needed to duplicate the usual haunting phenomena? And/or have the mental wherewithal to actually do something that requires intent? <br /> <br /> And that's plus the fact that they are super-easy pickings for Reapers who want to sell them down the river for soul-forging and, if they are mindlessly breaking the Dictum like that, a high priority target to boot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T10:09:28-07:00","id":1123056,"title":"","content":"what of spectres how rare are they supposed to be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T07:46:37-07:00","id":1123490,"title":"","content":"That's a complicated question and it really depends on what you mean. It's very hard to get a bead on their real numbers because of their high turnover rate, the ease with which many of them hide in Wraith society, and the strange hibernation cycles of the Labyrinth. In my understanding there are actually more Spectres than Wraiths, but that's only apparent when Maelstrom's hit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T04:06:58-07:00","id":1123825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1120879-what-is-stygia-s-legislation-on-thralls?p=1123490#post1123490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a complicated question and it really depends on what you mean. It's very hard to get a bead on their real numbers because of their high turnover rate, the ease with which many of them hide in Wraith society, and the strange hibernation cycles of the Labyrinth. In my understanding there are actually more Spectres than Wraiths, but that's only apparent when Maelstrom's hit.</div> </div> </div> </div>so for all we know some isolated necropoli might be literal &quot;cities full of spies&quot; or a village with &quot;a dark secret&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T04:39:37-07:00","id":1123830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1120879-what-is-stygia-s-legislation-on-thralls?p=1123825#post1123825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so for all we know some isolated necropoli might be literal &quot;cities full of spies&quot; or a village with &quot;a dark secret&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's a thing that could happen. In fact, it's viable enough that I bet there's Stygian propaganda about it. Renegade enclaves and Heretic cults could easily be called Spectres, and sometimes it might be accurate. Hierarchy outposts could be similarly compromised too, but Stygia is less likely to point that out.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 08-02-2017, 07:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T05:15:12-07:00","id":1123836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1120879-what-is-stygia-s-legislation-on-thralls?p=1123830#post1123830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, that's a thing that could happen. In fact, it's viable enough that I bet there's Stygian propaganda about it. Renegade enclaves and Heretic cults could easily be called Spectres, and sometimes it might be accurate. Hierarchy outposts could be similarly compromised too, but Stygia is less likely to point that out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've definitely run Wraith games where both have been true. I remember a Renegade group that was really pretty much a group of Specters and I recall the Grim Legion in another necropolis being suborned by Doppelgangers. <br /> <br /> The Hierarchy side would be less of a problem with a strong and independent Pardoners Guild. It would be like health care plans for the Legions with a little justified McCarthyism thrown in. &quot;Why doesn't the Anacreon ever see a Pardoner?&quot; would usually equate to &quot;Is the Anacreon a Doppelganger?&quot; In fact, a stronger, more visible and accessible Pardoners Guild would cause less issues with hidden Specters overall. <br /> <br /> I remember that I had the fairly small Silent Legion contingent trying to fulfill that role, as both Specter detectors and exterminators, (so, sort of Internal Affairs/Counseling, but with a Special Crimes/SWAT team flair) but they were spread mighty thin. <br /> <br /> Incidentally, and to the point of the original post, the Ashen Legion was the effectively in charge of rounding up the Drones for forging. Particularly since they had their Reapers at the local hospitals (and elderly care centers). They were supposed to allocate the Drones to the appropriate group, but there was some hanky-panky going on with them taking more than their fair share. The Emerald Legion, in particular, were on the receiving end of that. (And they, in turn, had their own job to do, which kept them occupied enough that they weren't able to always have their own Reapers around consistently...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}